Fixes in string and number functions that libc-test found: strtol and
its kin fail a base other than 0 or 2 to 36 with EINVAL instead of
reading digits in it (functional/strtol, wcstol); memmem and wcsstr
find an empty needle at the start of the haystack, as C and POSIX say
(string_memmem, wcsstr); and wctob gives back a byte above 127 as an
unsigned char, not a negative number (clocale_mbfuncs). Meant for
upstream.

diff -ruN a/options/ansi/generic/string.cpp b/options/ansi/generic/string.cpp
--- a/options/ansi/generic/string.cpp
+++ b/options/ansi/generic/string.cpp
@@ -419,6 +419,9 @@
 }
 
